{"assets":["/statement-assets/ecf78f4869d5d19cf4b43e8d7ca854d58c888177486c8ab1cab96bd8dd751b8a.png","/statement-assets/0587c821e4f7f5f1b91825587c8d1485c548d3715b1240efbcb00b3988997f27.png","/statement-assets/edb4adc5d93a9af2b8a3490c64dcc2d0aa59be1dd5d563d5e63a14d7b3a1212f.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1567","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Carrying Conundrum"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alice has just learned addition. However, she hasn't learned the concept of \"carrying\" fully — instead of carrying to the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"next"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" column, she carries to the column "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"two columns to the left"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"regular"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" way to evaluate the sum $$$2039 + 2976$$$ would be as shown: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/ecf78f4869d5d19cf4b43e8d7ca854d58c888177486c8ab1cab96bd8dd751b8a.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"However, Alice evaluates it as shown: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/0587c821e4f7f5f1b91825587c8d1485c548d3715b1240efbcb00b3988997f27.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In particular, this is what she does: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" add $$$9$$$ and $$$6$$$ to make $$$15$$$, and carry the $$$1$$$ to the column "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"two columns to the left"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", i. e. to the column \"$$$0$$$ $$$9$$$\"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" add $$$3$$$ and $$$7$$$ to make $$$10$$$ and carry the $$$1$$$ to the column "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"two columns to the left"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", i. e. to the column \"$$$2$$$ $$$2$$$\"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" add $$$1$$$, $$$0$$$, and $$$9$$$ to make $$$10$$$ and carry the $$$1$$$ to the column "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"two columns to the left"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", i. e. to the column above the plus sign; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" add $$$1$$$, $$$2$$$ and $$$2$$$ to make $$$5$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" add $$$1$$$ to make $$$1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" Thus, she ends up with the incorrect result of $$$15005$$$."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alice comes up to Bob and says that she has added two numbers to get a result of $$$n$$$. However, Bob knows that Alice adds in her own way. Help Bob find the number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ordered pairs of positive integers"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" such that when Alice adds them, she will get a result of $$$n$$$. Note that pairs $$$(a, b)$$$ and $$$(b, a)$$$ are considered different if $$$a \\ne b$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The input consists of multiple test cases. The first line contains an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 1000$$$) — the number of test cases. The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each test case contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\leq n \\leq 10^9$$$) — the number Alice shows Bob."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output one integer — the number of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ordered"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" pairs of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"positive integers"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" such that when Alice adds them, she will get a result of $$$n$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n100\n12\n8\n2021\n10000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n9\n4\n7\n44\n99\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, when Alice evaluates any of the sums $$$1 + 9$$$, $$$2 + 8$$$, $$$3 + 7$$$, $$$4 + 6$$$, $$$5 + 5$$$, $$$6 + 4$$$, $$$7 + 3$$$, $$$8 + 2$$$, or $$$9 + 1$$$, she will get a result of $$$100$$$. The picture below shows how Alice evaluates $$$6 + 4$$$: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/edb4adc5d93a9af2b8a3490c64dcc2d0aa59be1dd5d563d5e63a14d7b3a1212f.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1567C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1567/problem/C"}